# From Finite Windows to Infinite Symbolic Worlds

Chaotic motion can be read as an itinerary: each visit to one of two regions contributes a bit. This presentation explores how every infinite itinerary leaves a coherent family of finite shadows.

[Learn more about symbolic dynamics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_dynamics) and [de Bruijn graphs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Bruijn_graph).

## 1. Count the finite shadows

At depth $n$, there are exactly $2^n$ binary words. Increase the depth and watch the finite model grow.

