{{visualization:1}}

<details><summary>Reveal why truncation preserves every edge</summary>
An edge at word length $n+2$ supplies $n+1$ overlap equalities. After deleting each final symbol, the lower graph asks for only the first $n$ of those same equalities. No new condition is required.
</details>

