{{demo:1}}

## 3. Assemble the inverse limit

A compatible thread chooses one word of each length, with every shorter word obtained by deleting the last bit of the next. The whole thread is the collection of all finite prefixes of a trajectory.

{{interactive_demo:2}}

{{visualization:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal the trajectory-separation proof</summary>
If streams $s$ and $t$ differ at coordinate $k$, their prefixes of length $k+1$ differ at that coordinate. Therefore their inverse-limit threads are distinct. Conversely, equality at every prefix level forces equality of every coordinate.
</details>

